; Corrections to specific rows of the Bank A checking account exports, where
; the bank's category is wrong and no general pattern exists.
; Included at the end of import/bank_a__checking.rules, so these assignments
; override the import rules. Keyed on the bank reference, or on the date and
; label when a row has no reference.

; ==== Employer A wire mixing a salary bonus and an expense claim (split by hand)
if %reference ^2433559K10057514$
	account2 revenues:wages:employer-a:bank-wire
	amount2 -150,00
	account3 revenues:refunds:employer-a:expense-claims
	amount3 -42,30

; ==== Other recategorisations
; Bought at a bookshop, categorised by the bank as general shopping
if %reference ^2419359BP0002189$
	account2 expenses:discretionary:books
if
%date 21/08/2025
&& %libelle-simpl ^CB MARCHE DU SOIR$
	account2 expenses:essential:food:other
	comment market stall, categorised by the bank as a bar
